LLM_output:
To complete the right-hand side of the continuous assignment for `W_t`, we need to implement the message schedule expansion logic for SHA-256.

For rounds `t` from 16 to 63 (i.e., when `W_t` is being computed based on previous words), the `W_t` value is derived from the following formula:

$W_t = \sigma_1(W_{t-2}) + W_{t-7} + \sigma_0(W_{t-15}) + W_{t-16}$

Where:
*   `+` indicates addition modulo $2^{32}$.
*   `$\sigma_0(x)$` (small sigma 0) is defined as:
    $ROTR(x, 7) \oplus ROTR(x, 18) \oplus (x \gg 3)$
*   `$\sigma_1(x)$` (small sigma 1) is defined as:
    $ROTR(x, 17) \oplus ROTR(x, 19) \oplus (x \gg 10)$
*   `$ROTR(x, n)$` is the right rotation of `x` by `n` bits.
*   `$\gg$` is the logical right shift.
*   `$\oplus$` is the bitwise XOR operation.

The provided `reg [31:0] W_t_minus_XX;` variables directly correspond to the $W_{t-XX}$ terms in the formula.

Here's the completed Verilog code, including the necessary helper functions for rotation and the sigma operations:

```verilog
wire [31:0] W_t;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_01;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_02;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_03;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_04;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_05;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_06;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_07;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_08;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_09;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_10;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_11;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_12;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_13;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_14;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_15;
reg [31:0] W_t_minus_16;

// Helper function for Right Rotation (ROTR)
function [31:0] ROTR;
    input [31:0] x;
    input [5:0] n; // n can be up to 31, so 5 bits are enough for 0-31
    begin
        ROTR = (x >> n) | (x << (32 - n));
    end
endfunction

// Helper function for small sigma 0 (σ0)
// σ0(x) = ROTR(x, 7) ^ ROTR(x, 18) ^ (x >> 3)
function [31:0] sigma0;
    input [31:0] x;
    begin
        sigma0 = ROTR(x, 7) ^ ROTR(x, 18) ^ (x >> 3);
    end
endfunction

// Helper function for small sigma 1 (σ1)
// σ1(x) = ROTR(x, 17) ^ ROTR(x, 19) ^ (x >> 10)
function [31:0] sigma1;
    input [31:0] x;
    begin
        sigma1 = ROTR(x, 17) ^ ROTR(x, 19) ^ (x >> 10);
    end
endfunction

// Assign W_t based on the SHA-256 message schedule expansion formula
// W[t] = σ1(W[t-2]) + W[t-7] + σ0(W[t-15]) + W[t-16]
assign W_t = sigma1(W_t_minus_02) + W_t_minus_07 + sigma0(W_t_minus_15) + W_t_minus_16;
```

